00:05:43.945 --> 00:05:46.466
He's a wiz, man.
He knows all about this stuff, man.

00:05:46.466 --> 00:05:48.120
-Can we talk to wiz man?
-Yeah, let's go.

00:05:48.120 --> 00:05:49.970
Let's go talk to wiz man.
Cool, man.

00:05:51.155 --> 00:05:53.006
We were just sitting there
talking and stuff.

00:05:53.006 --> 00:05:55.863
And a Panther just come right
on his little dock, you know?

00:05:55.863 --> 00:05:58.094
Probably from here to the car away from us.

00:05:58.094 --> 00:05:59.181
A young one.

00:05:59.181 --> 00:06:00.806
And I was like what's up with that, man?

00:06:00.806 --> 00:06:03.600
He's like, he's been coming out
pretty recent, man. You know?

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:04.840
And pretty regular.

00:06:04.840 --> 00:06:05.979
I'm like, no sh*t, you know?

00:06:05.979 --> 00:06:08.555
So we're really not allowed
to feed him and stuff, so…

00:06:08.555 --> 00:06:10.300
-How are the dogs doing with the Panthers?

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:11.570
-You know, we look at them.

00:06:11.570 --> 00:06:12.780
Oh, they get at each other.

00:06:12.780 --> 00:06:14.326
The Panthers don't really bother them.

00:06:14.326 --> 00:06:16.976
He likes the little things,
the cats and the chickens.

00:06:17.219 --> 00:06:19.069
But… They're pretty cool, man.

00:06:19.813 --> 00:06:21.000
That's crazy, bro.

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:23.570
-I appreciate it.
-Yeah, man. That's pretty cool, man.

00:06:23.570 --> 00:06:26.580
So if I came here on my own,
I might have had a different response.

00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:27.580
Oh, yeah. Nah.

00:06:28.264 --> 00:06:29.340
It's a joke. 

00:06:29.340 --> 00:06:30.340
Hey, Uncle Scott.

00:06:30.810 --> 00:06:32.698
You never know
what you're going to get into.

00:06:32.698 --> 00:06:34.427
-Sleeping?
-I'm trying to.

00:06:34.427 --> 00:06:35.885
Alright, sorry about that.

00:06:36.219 --> 00:06:37.719
I'll see you after while, Unc.

00:06:37.998 --> 00:06:39.280
We just talked to Billy.

00:06:39.280 --> 00:06:40.560
-The old Black guy?
-Yeah.

00:06:40.560 --> 00:06:42.366
Yeah, he's awesome, man.
Good guy.

00:06:42.366 --> 00:06:44.622
So, living out here.

00:06:44.622 --> 00:06:46.722
-Yes, sir.
-Separated from the world feeling.

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:49.393
Basically, it is a little different.

00:06:49.394 --> 00:06:52.644
I mean, you got, seems
a little more freedom, maybe, I should say.

00:06:53.270 --> 00:06:56.480
You know, you don't really get bothered
by many people unless you act a fool.

00:06:56.481 --> 00:06:58.393
I mean, it's freedom, bro.

00:06:58.818 --> 00:07:00.200
What you see is what it is.

00:07:00.200 --> 00:07:02.000
-Alright.
-Everybody knows everybody.

00:07:02.468 --> 00:07:04.222
It reminds me of the old days, you know?

00:07:04.222 --> 00:07:06.584
Where you can go to your neighbor
and borrow an egg.

00:07:06.591 --> 00:07:10.260
Nowadays you go to the city, they'll shut
the door on you and won't answer.

00:07:10.260 --> 00:07:12.778
A little different.
But, yeah, man, it's pretty cool.

00:07:13.130 --> 00:07:15.368
I'd like to take you guys somewhere
and show you more.

00:07:16.300 --> 00:07:18.800
I'm going to close this gate here.
My uncle's gate.

00:07:19.359 --> 00:07:21.305
And then I'm going to go find my brother

00:07:21.305 --> 00:07:23.153
and we're going to show
you some good videos.

00:07:23.153 --> 00:07:25.268
-Where's your brother?
-He's right across the way.

00:07:25.268 --> 00:07:26.660
We're going to follow you.

00:07:26.660 --> 00:07:28.184
-Let's go.
-Okay. Okay.

00:07:30.398 --> 00:07:32.018
[Brian calling out]

00:07:37.372 --> 00:07:40.383
[Brian] He wants to know about
the woods and all that sh*t, man.

00:07:40.383 --> 00:07:42.710
-How are you doing, sir?
-He's good f*cking people, man.

00:07:42.710 --> 00:07:44.670
